            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear Colleague, I am writing to summarise the recent inpatient episode of your patient, a 67-year-old female, admitted on 10 September 2026 with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray excluded pneumonia or pneumothorax. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed type 1 respiratory failure. Blood tests showed a mild inflammatory response. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen, with good clinical response. Oxygen saturations normalised and she was mobilised with physiotherapy support. She received education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation action plans. She is discharged home in stable condition. Please arrange follow-up and review of her inhaler regimen. Do not hesitate to contact me with any queries.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
